{{en-noun}}

# An [[act#Noun|act]] of [[hand out|handing out]] something.
## {{lb|en|US|card games|archaic|rare}} An act of [[deal#Verb|dealing]] [[playing card]]s; a [[deal#Noun|deal]].
# {{senseid|en|printed sheet}} A [[printed#Adjective|printed]] [[sheet#Noun|sheet]] such as a [[leaflet#Noun|leaflet]] or [[pamphlet#Noun|pamphlet]], or a [[worksheet]], that is [[give out|given out]] [[free of charge]] (usually [[by hand]]) for a [[certain#Determiner|certain]] [[use#Noun|use]], for example as an [[advertisement]] or for [[information]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Jeane W. Anastas|chapter=Teaching Courses: Methods and Modalities|title=Teaching in Social Work: An Educators’ Guide to Theory and Practice|location=New York, N.Y.&#59; Chichester, West Sussex|publisher=w:Columbia University Press|year=2010|page=39|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=x4C-AwAAQBAJ&pg=PA39|isbn=978-0-231-11524-7|passage=Therefore, it is often recommended that the framework or outline for a lecture be provided to students on the chalkboard or in a '''handout''' so they can more easily follow the logic as the lecture progresses.}}
## {{synonym of|en|press release|t=an [[official#Adjective|official]] [[written#Adjective|written]] [[statement#Noun|statement]] that is [[send#Verb|sent]] to the [[media#Noun 2|media]] so that it can be [[publicize]]d}}
# {{senseid|en|a gift to the poor or needy}} {{lb|en|often|derogatory}} A [[gift#Noun|gift]] of [[money#Noun|money]] or [[material#Adjective|material]] [[assistance]] to the [[needy]] or [[poor#Noun|poor]].
#: {{synonyms|en|bonsella<q:South Africa>}}
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Oakdale Affair|year=2003|page=19|passage=We ain't runnin' no day nursery. These you see here is all the real thing. Maybe we asks fer a '''handout''' now and then; but that ain't our reg'lar lay.}}
#* {{RQ:Cather Professor's House|chapter=III|page=196|passage=They dropped old Henry at Tarpin, where he soon drank up all his wages. When Rapp picked him up there, he was living on '''hand-outs'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|writers=w:Ethan Coen; w:Joel Coen|actor=w:David Huddleston|role=Jeffrey “The Big” Lebowski|title=w:The Big Lebowski|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240704110843/http://web.mit.edu/putz/Public/big_lebowski.txt|location=United States|publisher={{w|Gramercy Pictures}}; [[w:PolyGram Filmed Entertainment|PolyGram Films International]]|date=18 January 1998|oclc=41312447|passage=You're just looking for a '''handout''' like every other—are you employed, Mr. Lebowski?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Chloe Schwenke|chapter=Introduction|title=Reclaiming Value in International Development: The Moral Dimensions of Development Policy and Practice in Poor Countries|location=Westport, Conn.|publisher=Praeger Publishers, {{w|Greenwood Publishing Group}}|year=2009|page=1|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=4OfEEAAAQBAJ&pg=PA1|isbn=978-0-313-36332-0|passage=A woman, dressed in simple and worn clothes, holding a very young and rather dirty looking baby, was seeking a '''handout'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Geneva Abdul|title=Liz Truss rejects ‘handouts’ as way to tackle cost of living crisis|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240708184736/https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2022/aug/06/liz-truss-handouts-cost-of-living-crisis-tax-cuts-conservative-leadership|date=6 August 2022|passage=With mounting pressure as households face a financial squeeze, the foreign secretary rejected '''handouts''' and insisted on tax cuts costing more than £30bn as the country spirals towards a recession. "Of course I will look at what more can be done," [[w:Liz Truss|{{quote-gloss|Liz}} Truss]] told the Financial Times. "But the way I would do things is in a Conservative way of lowering the tax burden, not giving out '''handouts'''."}}
## {{lb|en|by extension}} Something [[obtain]]ed without [[effort#Noun|effort]]; a gift, a [[present#Noun|present]].
##: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:gift}}
##* {{RQ:Guardian|author=[[w:Daniel Taylor (journalist)|Daniel Taylor]]|title={{w|Sergio Agüero}} strike wins derby for [[w:Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] against 10-man [[w:Manchester United F.C.|United]]|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230614214532/http://www.theguardian.com/football/2014/nov/02/manchester-city-manchester-united-premier-league-match-report|date=2 November 2014|passage=They {{quote-gloss|Manchester United}} had contributed heavily to their own downfall, most glaringly with the senselessness of {{w|Chris Smalling}}'s red card, and they should know by now that {{w|Manuel Pellegrini}}'s team are not the kind of opponents to pass up these kind of '''handouts'''.}}

====Usage notes====
In current use, {{senseno|en|a gift to the poor or needy}} (“gift of money or material assistance to the needy or poor”) often carries the derogatory connotation that the recipient does not deserve the gift.<ref name="OED"/>

